  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 345 AM EDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nNot a whole lot of changes to the going forecast. Rain showers \ncontinue over northern IL into central MI this morning with the\nband of showers on the northwest periphery of ridging further \nsouth and east which will mainly keep the introduction of rain \nshowers for areas closer to Lake Michigan into this afternoon \nas the lower levels further moisten. WPC has a marginal risk for\nexcessive rainfall for later today and as the ridging pushes \nfurther south and east rain showers will make their way further \nsouth and east through Friday morning with a slight risk for \nexcessive rainfall for tomorrow. A few embedded thunderstorms \nwill be possible with the southern and eastward push but at this\ntime severe weather is not anticipated. \n\nA more zonal aloft pattern emerges across the region this\nweekend and will bring a return to dry conditions and cooler\ntemperatures especially into the beginning of next week when\nhighs will only get to around 60 degrees both Monday and\nTuesday.",
